        "type": "p",
        "text": "Typing your own practice type and city into Google tells you almost nothing reliable. Google personalizes results by your location, your search history and the device in your hand, and local results change from one street to the next. Someone two miles away may see a different top three. You also tend to find your own practice faster than a stranger would, because Google already knows you visit your site. A single manual check is a data point about you, not about your patients."
